# build output
dist/
# generated types
.astro/
# dependencies
node_modules/
# environment
.env
.env.production

# Real image assets under public/ are tracked (root .gitignore ignores *.png globally)
!public/og-image.png
# The touch icon is an asset the page links, not a screenshot. Same trap the
# canon covers hit: the root `*.png` rule swallows it, `git add` says nothing,
# and the icon 404s on the deployed site only.
!public/apple-touch-icon.png
# Canon cover art is page content, not a stray screenshot. Without this the root
# rule swallows a PNG jacket dropped into the bookcase's art directory: `git add`
# reports nothing, and the cover falls back to its printed face on the deployed
# page only. JPEGs were never caught by that rule, which is why the first four
# covers landed and a fifth in PNG would not have.
!public/canon/*.png
